{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And by the chariot:</b> Now in the three chariots he mentioned horses with a single eye each, and this one differs from that — red, black, and white. But in the fourth he mentioned two colors: spotted, and also amutzim, from the root אמץ, which is a strong color, visible from afar more than all colors."], :book :zechariah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zecharia -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zecharya"] ["1" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=25&perek=5&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:46:06.545718824Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}